      "id": 1,
      "text": "Rock City Falls began when brothers Daniel and Valentine Rathbun built one of the first mills in the late 1700s, later becoming the Kilmer Stone Mill.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.news10.com/news/saratoga-county/the-history-of-rock-city-falls/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1902 the Empire Mill was sold to Edward Brown and renamed Brown’s Paper Mill, marking a new chapter in the hamlet’s industrial history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.news10.com/news/saratoga-county/the-history-of-rock-city-falls/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "From 1898 to 1929 the Ballston Terminal Railroad, an electric trolley, hauled freight for the paper mills and carried passengers to Ballston Spa.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rock_City_Falls%2C_New_York",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The George West House, a historic home in Rock City Falls, earned a spot on the National Register of Historic Places in 2005.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
